{"format":"mathslides","version":1,"deck":{"version":1,"id":"YXydyjxHMW","title":"Untitled presentation","slides":[{"id":"nfhk_Gh3Pu","background":"#ffffff","elements":[{"id":"mW7Lub6mOY","type":"text","x":96,"y":210,"w":1088,"h":108,"doc":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Untitled presentation"}]}]},"style":{"fontSize":80,"color":"#000000","align":"center","lineHeight":1.35,"fill":null}},{"id":"pHqFjq_d4X","type":"text","x":96,"y":350,"w":1088,"h":41,"doc":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"내용은 빈 곳을 클릭해 텍스트를 쓰고, /math 로 수식을 넣어 보세요"}]}]},"style":{"fontSize":30,"color":"#404040","align":"center","lineHeight":1.35,"fill":null}}],"notes":"","reference":"","kind":"title"},{"id":"K5iAdu_Up9","background":"#ffffff","elements":[{"id":"IsBdmtGZL2","type":"text","x":64,"y":40,"w":1152,"h":68,"doc":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"슬라이드 제목"}]}]},"style":{"fontSize":50,"color":"#000000","align":"left","lineHeight":1.35,"fill":null}},{"id":"cpL4snEyLr","type":"text","x":64,"y":132,"w":1152,"h":41,"doc":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"내용을 입력하세요"}]}]},"style":{"fontSize":30,"color":"#000000","align":"left","lineHeight":1.35,"fill":null}},{"id":"zARaW73ULg","type":"text","x":130,"y":220,"w":999,"h":43,"doc":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"From PPO to GRPO"}]}]},"style":{"fontSize":32,"color":"#000000","align":"left","lineHeight":1.35,"fill":null}},{"id":"gt3-iN9RE4","type":"text","x":8,"y":285,"w":1264,"h":43,"doc":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Proximal Policy Optimization (PPO) (Schulman et al., 2017) is an actor-critic RL algorithm that is widely used in the RL fine-tuning stage of LLMs (Ouyang et al., 2022). In particular, it optimizes LLMs by maximizing the following surrogate objective:"}]}]},"style":{"fontSize":16,"color":"#000000","align":"left","lineHeight":1.35,"fill":null}},{"id":"CuwcvNrK3N","type":"text","x":106,"y":369,"w":1074,"h":76,"doc":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"mathBlock","attrs":{"latex":"\\\\(J_{PPO}(\\theta) = \\mathbb{E}[q \\sim P(Q), o \\sim \\pi_{\\theta_{old}}(O|q)] \\frac{1}{|o|} \\sum_{t=1}^{|o|} \\min \\left[ \\frac{\\pi_{\\theta}(o_t|q, o_{<t})}{\\pi_{\\theta_{old}}(o_t|q, o_{<t})} A_t, \\text{clip} \\left( \\frac{\\pi_{\\theta}(o_t|q, o_{<t})}{\\pi_{\\theta_{old}}(o_t|q, o_{<t})}, 1-\\varepsilon, 1+\\varepsilon \\right) A_t \\right],"}}]},"style":{"fontSize":20,"color":"#000000","align":"center","lineHeight":1.35,"fill":null}},{"id":"HxhUlhgi3D","type":"text","x":8,"y":470,"w":1264,"h":65,"doc":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"where \\("},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"\\pi"}},{"type":"text","text":"_{"},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"\\theta"}},{"type":"text","text":"}\\) and \\("},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"\\pi"}},{"type":"text","text":"_{"},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"\\theta"}},{"type":"text","text":"_{old}}\\) are the current and old policy models, and \\(q, o\\) are questions and outputs sampled from the question dataset and the old policy \\("},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"\\pi"}},{"type":"text","text":"_{"},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"\\theta"}},{"type":"text","text":"_{old}}\\), respectively. \\("},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"\\varepsilon"}},{"type":"text","text":"\\) is a clipping-related hyper-parameter introduced in PPO for stabilizing training. \\(A_t\\) is the advantage, which is computed by applying Generalized Advantage Estimation (GAE) (Schulman et al., 2015), based"}]}]},"style":{"fontSize":16,"color":"#000000","align":"left","lineHeight":1.35,"fill":null}}],"notes":"","reference":""}],"titleElementId":"mW7Lub6mOY"},"assets":{}}